{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\n// Defined in habeas_sdk::graph.\npub enum EvidenceState<O> {\n    Current(O),\n    Missing,\n    Stale,\n}\n\n// Method on Validator<'d, D>.\npub fn check<V: Validation<D>>(\n    &self,\n    validation: &V,\n) -> impl Future<Output = Result<EvidenceState<V::Ok>, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n```\n\n`check` uses the same identity, revision, and freshness comparison as `verify`.\nIt reads the descriptor before awaiting; it does not retain a reference to the\nvalidation value across asynchronous storage or dependency operations. Checking\ninvokes neither `execute` nor a model and writes no evidence. It needs no\nconfigured agent. Storage, dependency-resolution, and current-output decoding\nfailures are errors, not missing or stale evidence.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.validation.check_node`, and I found no gap. I did not need implementation source.\n\n- **Same comparison as `verify`.**\n  - The tests assert `Current`, `Missing` and `Stale` outcomes.\n  - `Current` cases: `criteria_have_independent_typed_answers_and_cache_negative_results`, `changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another`, and `runner_reuses_negative_judgments_and_records_only_callback_observations`.\n  - `Missing` cases: a different criterion, a different source node, and an unverified criterion. These are in `wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes` and the `criteria_have_independent_typed_answers_and_cache_negative_results` test.\n  - `Stale` cases: a dependency change (`changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another`) and a revision change (`revision_and_dependency_checks_precede_output_decoding` and `runner_reuses_negative_judgments_and_records_only_callback_observations`).\n  - The stored `*` revision case is covered too.\n  - A sibling criterion stays `Current` when another one goes stale.\n- **No retained reference or reads before awaiting.** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` drives `check` through a `send(...)` helper with a non-`Sync` `Review`. It also asserts `descriptor_reads == 1`.\n- **No `execute`, no model, no writes.** The tests assert execution and write counters after checks. They also assert that a `Missing` check in `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` leaves the evidence file absent and sends no provider request. They assert the stored bytes are unchanged after a `Current` check. `revision_and_dependency_checks_precede_output_decoding` shows `writes == 1` after a `Stale` check.\n- **No agent needed.** Checks in most of these tests run on validators built without an agent.\n- **Errors, not `Missing` or `Stale`.**\n  - Load failures are covered in `loading_execution_resolution_and_saving_failures_do_not_publish_answers`.\n  - Dependency read and edge failures are covered in `dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers`.\n  - Malformed storage (a `Json` error) and an undecodable current output (`ValidationError::Output`) are covered in the `storage.rs` test `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_current_bad_outputs_are_output_errors`. `revision_and_dependency_checks_precede_output_decoding` covers the `Output` case as well.\n\nAll the tests carry `{test}` references to the subject, so there are no marking gaps.",
